![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

In `resolve_network`, when resolving a network object group, the resolved set of IP addresses/networks is returned directly without being cached in `self._network_cache`. This means that network object groups are never cached, causing them to be re-resolved from scratch on every call. This can be a significant performance bottleneck for large configurations with nested groups. 

Additionally, because they are never cached, the `self._network_cache.pop(key, None)` cleanup logic for cyclic groups is currently a no-op for object groups. To fix this and improve performance, we should cache the resolved set in `self._network_cache` before returning.

